      "title": "How to Use This Guide",
      "content": "## **How to Use This Guide** \n\nThis guide is built like a field manual. Read one page per day, then act. Money improves when attention becomes a system: track, decide, automate, review, and repeat. \n\n### **Important disclaimer** \n\nThis is educational material only. It is not personal investment, tax, legal, or insurance advice. Your income, country, family responsibilities, debts, taxes, and risk tolerance matter. For major decisions, consult qualified professionals. \n\n#### **The one rule** \n\nDo not try to look rich. Build the ability to stay free, useful, calm, and financially resilient. \n\n### **Core reference base** \n\n- OECD: financial literacy as awareness, knowledge, skills, attitudes, and behaviours for informed financial decisions. \n\n- Reserve Bank of India financial education resources: budgeting, saving, good financial practices, digital awareness, and consumer protection. \n\n- U.S. Federal Reserve education: money supply includes currency and bank balances used for payments and short-term stores of value. \n\n- SEC Investor.gov: compound interest and diversification basics for retail investors. \n\n- SEBI investor education material: savings, investments, income, expenditure, and investor awareness."
