      "moduleNumber": 1,
      "moduleTitle": "Foundation: What Money Really Is",
      "title": "Table of Contents",
      "content": "## **Table of Contents** \n\n#### Module 1: Foundation: What Money Really Is \n\n1. Money is stored life energy, 2. The four jobs of money, 3. Price is a signal, 4. Income is a stream, wealth is a reservoir, 5. Cash flow beats appearance, 6. Inflation quietly changes reality, 7. Liquidity is survival power, 8. Risk is not the enemy, 9. Time changes money, 10. Financial literacy is behavior plus knowledge \n\n#### Module 2: Flow of Money: How the System Moves \n\n1. Money moves in circuits, 2. Banks are money channels, 3. Credit expands activity, 4. Interest is the price of time and risk, 5. Government money flow, 6. Business cash conversion, 7. Capital markets allocate ownership, 8. Global money flow, 9. Velocity matters, 10. Follow incentives, not speeches \n\n#### Module 3: What Schools and Colleges Usually Miss \n\n1. Salary is only one money engine, 2. Your degree is not your financial plan, 3. Marks do not teach markets, 4. Nobody grades your lifestyle inflation, 5. Debt has psychology, 6. Taxes shape outcomes, 7. Negotiation is a money skill, 8. Accounting is the language of money, 9. Personal finance is not personal weakness, 10. Financial education must be applied \n\n#### Module 4: Analyzing Money: Personal, Business, and Economy \n\n1. The personal cash-flow statement, 2. Net worth is your scoreboard, 3. The balance sheet mindset, 4. The income statement mindset, 5. The cash-flow mindset, 6. Ratio analysis for life, 7. Opportunity cost, 8. Risk-adjusted return, 9. Scenario analysis, 10. Decision journals \n\n#### Module 5: Money Mindset and Behavior \n\n1. Money needs respect, not worship, 2. Scarcity vs discipline, 3. Identity drives spending, 4. Delayed gratification is power, 5. Emotions tax returns, 6. Comparison is expensive, 7. Money conversations matter, 8. Confidence must be earned, 9. Frugality is strategic, 10. Abundance requires capability \n\n#### Module 6: Power of Money \n\n1. Money buys options, 2. Money amplifies character, 3. Ownership creates influence, 4. Capital attracts opportunity, 5. Reputation converts to money, 6. Networks move money, 7. Knowledge compounds, 8. Leverage magnifies output, 9. Money and freedom, 10. Power needs principles \n\n#### Module 7: Making Money Work for You \n\n1. Pay yourself first, 2. Build an emergency fund, 3. Clear bad debt strategically, 4. Invest consistently, 5. Use compounding patiently, 6. Diversify intelligently, 7. Keep costs low, 8. Increase earning power, 9. Create asset-producing systems, 10. Review and rebalance \n\n#### Module 8: Earning More: Skills, Career, and Business \n\n1. Solve expensive problems, 2. Document proof of work, 3. Learn sales ethically, 4. Pricing is positioning, 5. Freelance cash-flow discipline, 6. Build multiple income lanes, 7. Career capital, 8. Negotiating salary, 9. Business model thinking, 10. Scale through systems \n\n#### Module 9: Protecting Money \n\n1. Insurance protects the base, 2. Avoid fraud and hype, 3. Protect digital money, 4. Legal documents matter, 5. Tax planning is not evasion, 6. Avoid concentration risk, 7. Protect your time, 8. Health is financial infrastructure, 9. Protect relationships, 10. Build resilience \n\n#### Module 10: Advanced Thinking: Investing, Cycles, and Strategy \n\n1. Asset classes have roles, 2. Understand market cycles, 3. Valuation matters, 4. Margin of safety, 5. Behavioral edge, 6. Information diet, 7. Systems beat predictions, 8. The barbell approach, 9. Human capital allocation, 10. Strategy is choosing trade-offs \n\n#### Module 11: 90-Day Money Operating System"
