      "title": "Appendix B: 30 Money Rules Worth Keeping",
      "content": "## **Appendix B: 30 Money Rules Worth Keeping** \n\n1. Spend less than you earn before trying advanced strategies. \n\n2. Emergency fund before speculation. \n\n3. Never confuse EMI affordability with wealth. \n\n4. Do not invest money needed soon in volatile assets. \n\n5. Avoid lifestyle upgrades until savings rate is stable. \n\n6. Insurance is for catastrophic risk, not small inconvenience. \n\n7. Track net worth monthly. \n\n8. Raise income through skill, proof, and negotiation. \n\n9. Learn basic tax rules in your country. \n\n10. Do not buy assets you cannot explain. \n\n11. Do not lend money you cannot emotionally afford to lose. \n\n12. Keep financial records organized. \n\n13. Beware guaranteed high returns. \n\n14. Diversify income and investments. \n\n15. Understand fees before investing. \n\n16. Use automation to defeat forgetfulness. \n\n17. Do not make big decisions when angry, afraid, or desperate. \n\n18. Value liquidity during uncertain periods. \n\n19. Invest in health and skills early. \n\n20. Make money conversations clear and written. \n\n21. Avoid comparing your financial life to visible lifestyle. \n\n22. Use debt mainly for productive or necessary purposes. \n\n23. Review subscriptions quarterly. \n\n24. Invest regularly, not dramatically. \n\n25. Build a portfolio of proof for career growth. \n\n26. Protect accounts with strong security. \n\n27. Keep fixed costs low when changing careers. \n\n28. Study business models around you. \n\n29. Choose freedom over status. \n\n30. Become more valuable every year."
